      "text": {{ JSON.stringify("Analyze this script data and return emotions for each line, character traits, AND practice segments for user lines.

CHARACTERS:
" + JSON.stringify($json.characters) + "

LINES:
" + JSON.stringify($json.linesForEmotion) + "

Return JSON:
{
  "emotions": ["emotion1", "emotion2", ...],
  "characters": [{"name": "UPPERCASE", "age_range": "child|teen|young_adult|adult|mature|elderly", "archetype": "protagonist|mentor|authority|friend|love_interest|comic_relief|antagonist|supporting", "vocal_quality": "warm|sharp|soft|commanding|energetic|calm|gravelly|bright"}],
  "segments": {"LINE_INDEX": ["segment1", "segment2", ...], ...}
}

EMOTION RULES:
- Emotions array must match lines array length and order
- Options: neutral, happy, sad, angry, excited, fearful, surprised, whisper, shouting, sarcastic, nervous, confident, pleading, menacing, tender, bitter, hopeful
- Parentheticals are hints: (angrily)=angry, (softly)=tender, (whispered)=whisper
- Action/narrator lines = neutral
- Default to neutral if unclear

CHARACTER TRAIT RULES:
- age_range: Dr./Detective/Officer titles = adult+, interns/residents = young_adult, parents of teens = mature
- archetype: Base on role in scene - who drives action (protagonist), who guides (mentor), who opposes (antagonist)
- vocal_quality: Match personality from dialogue - nervous speakers = soft, authority figures = commanding, friendly = warm

SEGMENT RULES (USER CHARACTER LINES ONLY):
- Only generate segments for lines where character has is_user_character: true
- segments object keys are the line idx (as string)
- MINIMUM segment size: 3 words. NEVER create a segment with fewer than 3 words
- If splitting at a sentence boundary would create a segment under 3 words, merge it with the previous segment
- Split at natural actor breath/thought points: sentence endings (. ! ?), clauses (, ; : --)
- Segment length MUST be 3-5 words. Never exceed 5 words per segment.
- Preserve emotional beats -- don't split mid-thought
- Short lines (under 5 words) = single segment with full text
- Never create segments that are ONLY filler sounds (um, uh, sigh, etc.) -- merge them with the following words
- GOOD example: idx 5, text "I know I might look too young, but I studied hard. I earned this."
  Result: {"5": ["I know I might look too young,", "but I studied hard. I earned this."]}
- BAD example: {"5": ["I'm fine.", "Thanks."]} -- "Thanks." is 1 word. Correct: {"5": ["I'm fine. Thanks."]}
- BAD example: {"5": ["I know I might look too young,", "but I studied hard.", "I earned this."]} -- "I earned this." is 3 words but could merge with previous. Prefer fewer, meatier segments") }}
    }]
  }],
  "generationConfig": {
    "temperature": 0.1,
    "maxOutputTokens": 4096,
    "responseMimeType": "application/json"
  }
}

